You decide to go over Niagara Falls in abarrel, but all such stunts became illegalin 1961 and you are arrested. You lose twohours but don't break your neck.The first wave of immigrants landed atEllis Island in 1932.20Vertigo strikes while you are crossing theBrooklyn Bridge, once the longest suspensionbridge in the world. You lose an hour while afriend urges you to continue and not look down.Grand Central Terminal is famous for beingmore than just a train station. It was oncethe largest enclosed space in the world.11You go jogging at the Reservoir in CentralPark hoping to spot a celebrity. Instead ofcatching a glimpse of Woody Allen or Spike Lee,you see Harry meet Sally and lose one hour.Liberty Island, which contains the Statue ofLiberty, was a quarantine station, the site ofFort Wood, and a place for hanging pirates.11You drive up to Ithaca for your sister, whowants you to reclaim her record collection from her former roommate, now a graduatestudent at Cornell. Lose two hours.In 1901, schoolteacher Annie Taylor wasthe first person to successfully go overNiagara Falls in a barrel. People are stilltrying to break her speed record.20Harry wants a first-edition copy of "RipVan Winkle." When you finally locate it, hewon't pay the price. You lose two hours drivingto the Catskills just to buy the paperback."The Borscht Belt" is the name for a stringof hotels along the southern rim of theCatskill Mountains.21Lazar tells you to send a Mets pennant to Harry. After you mail it, you learn Harry is a Jets, not a Mets, fan. He detests theMets. You lose two hours awaiting his wrath.Cooperstown, New York in the Adirondacks iswhere American football was invented.20You sneak to Flushing Meadows to watch JohnMcEnroe throw a tantrum at the U.S. Open. Harry wouldn't have known if you hadn't lostyour press pass on the subway. Lose an hour.King Kong clinging to the Empire StateBuilding is one of the most famous images ofNew York. To this day he is the only creature tohave climbed a New York skyscraper.10You sprain your finger trying on a two-caratdiamond at Tiffany's. Lose two hours icing your finger and your credit card.Trump Tower, located next to Tiffany & Co., is a rent-controlled apartment complex. The stores there accept student and senior- citizen discounts.20You faint underneath Radio City Music Hall'schandeliers when you learn they are thelargest in the world at two tons each. No onecan find smelling salts. Lose an hour.Staten Island, one of the five sectionscalled "boroughs" that make up New York City, was given away as a prize.11Harry wants a Hard Rock Cafe T-shirt. You volunteer to stand in line and get to shake hands with James Brown. You feel good but lose two hours.Boss Tweed and the Tammany Hall society ranNew York City as well as the state during the1860s and 70s. This period is rememberedfor democracy at its best.20